# LLM Backend — Ollama configuration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env and adjust values to match your setup.
# .env is git-ignored and never committed.
#
# All variables are optional. The pipeline works on a stock local Ollama
# install with no configuration at all — the only variable you typically
# need to set is OLLAMA_MODEL (to match what you have pulled).
#
# See docs/llm_setup.md for installation instructions and model recommendations.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of the running Ollama instance.
# Change if Ollama is on a different host or port.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434

# Model tag — must match exactly what `ollama list` shows.
# Pull the model first: ollama pull qwen2.5:7b
OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3-vl:8b

# Advanced parameters — leave commented out unless you need to tune them.
# OLLAMA_TIMEOUT=600.0      # per-request timeout in seconds (allow for cold model load)
# OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=8192       # context window in tokens (increase for very long sections)
# OLLAMA_TEMPERATURE=0.0    # 0.0 = deterministic output (recommended)
